Z||000000||pHoOl||10-12-2000||08:25 PM||||While i was cruzing Meijer today (don't know if there are any outside of michigan, but it's basically an all purpose store) i saw one of those "PONTIAC" windshield stickers for sale, the one that goes where the blue part of the glass is.  To make a short story boring, i put it inside and notice that from the outside, you can't tell it's even there.<P>I checked the directions and i had followed them to the T.  For the time being, i put it on the outside, so i'll see if it stays.  It's made of that material that isn't sticky but will stick from static electricity.  They probably call that kind of thing "vinel" or however you spell it.  (thank God i'm not an english major)<P>Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||10-12-2000||08:43 PM||||I did that too. It will not stay on the outside, mine came off with highway speeds on the way in town. I went to a local sign shop and they made me one to stick on the outside of the windshield for $20. I put it on and it looks great, and have washed the car countless times alreay and not trouble. I will try and get a pict tonight if I can. If your interested I could get one made for you.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-12-2000||08:58 PM||||I bought one of those and put it in the back window, it cuts down on the headlights beaming in the back window.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||pHoOl||10-12-2000||09:59 PM||||I had a guy today that told me he knows of a place that makes them locally.  I kinda wanted to keep it somewhat temporary.  But maybe that's not an option.  Thanks for the help guys.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
